1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Here’s how fast-forwarding works in TestingView.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:09,000
First, I’m stepping forward by minute: perfect when you want precision.

3
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:14,560
Now I’ll open Settings
and change the Minimum Step Forward.

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,100
This controls Step Forward and Fast Forward speed.

5
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,400
Let’s switch it from 1 minute to 5 minutes.

6
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,060
Smaller steps - more precision.
Bigger steps - faster movement.

7
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:30,900
Now when I step forward, watch the time bottom-right:
it jumps 5 minutes at a time.

8
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:37,220
Next, fast forward:
choose the interval, then click Fast Forward.

9
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,780
Notice it won’t teleport mid-candle.

10
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:47,720
Here we’re at 17:29,
so it goes to the candle close first: 17:59

11
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:54,000
Then it continues forward -
keeping candle states accurate while you move faster.
